# Testing and package edits

- Pest + Orchestra Testbench. Helper: `renderSeo(SEOData $input)` in `tests/Pest.php`.
- Suites: `TagManagerInputDataTest` (normalize), `TagSuiteTest` (HTML), `SchemaSuiteTest` (JSON-LD), `BladeDirectivesTest` (`@seo`/`@seoData`), `SEOServiceTest` (singleton / empty fallback).
- `composer test:unit` expects 100% coverage. Run relevant Pest filters after behavior changes.

```php
$output = renderSeo(new SEOData(title: 'My title', url: 'https://example.com/post'));
expect($output)->toContain('<title>My title</title>');
```

## Extending the package

1. Add a field to `SEOData` only if cross-cutting.
2. Wire it in `TagManager` (field → markup).
3. Document it in `.cursor/rules/seo-data.mdc`.
4. Add Pest for render + normalize edge cases.
5. Keep examples aligned with real ctor + `@seo` / `@seoData` (not outdated README APIs).

Escape via `TagManager` `el()` / `e()`. Named ctor args / current PHP style.
